# .arcus-ignore
#
# This file specifies files/folders that ARCUS agents should COMPLETELY IGNORE
# when analysing project structure and generating .context/ artifacts or
# copilot-instructions.md.
#
# WHAT "IGNORE" MEANS:
#   - Files/folders matching these patterns are EXCLUDED from all analysis
#   - They will NOT be mentioned in copilot-instructions.md
#   - They will NOT appear in feature lists, module tables, flow files, or any
#     generated documentation
#   - They are treated as if they don't exist in the repository
#
# WHEN IT APPLIES:
#   - /sdd.context-builder  — scanning the repo to generate .context/
#   - /sdd.instructions     — scanning the repo to generate copilot-instructions.md
#   - /sdd.specify          — context drift reconciliation before specifying
#   - Any agent that calls context/context-sync or foundation/repository-context-builder
#
# USE CASES:
#   - Exclude dependencies (node_modules/, vendor/)
#   - Exclude build artifacts (dist/, build/, target/)
#   - Exclude framework/tooling files that aren't your application code
#   - Exclude ARCUS framework directories (.arcus/, .github/agents/, .github/skills/)
#
# SYNTAX:
#   - Lines starting with # are comments
#   - Each line specifies one pattern, matched against paths relative to repo root
#   - Use / as the directory separator
#   - Trailing / indicates a directory (all contents ignored)
#   - *  matches any sequence of characters (except /)
#   - ** matches any sequence of characters (including /)
#   - Blank lines are ignored
#
# EXAMPLES:
#   node_modules/       — ignore the node_modules directory and everything in it
#   dist/               — ignore build output
#   *.log               — ignore all log files anywhere in the repo
#   temp/**             — ignore temp directory and all subdirectories
#   **/*.min.js         — ignore all minified JS files anywhere in the repo
#
# CUSTOMISATION:
#   This file is copied once on first integration and is yours to edit.
#   Re-running `arcus-integrate --sync` will NOT overwrite your customisations.
#   Add project-specific exclusions below the default entries.

# ─── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
vendor/
venv/
env/
.env/
.venv/

# ─── Build outputs and generated files ───────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
out/
target/
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.bundle.js
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.class

# ─── IDE and editor files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── Version control ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.svn/
.hg/

# ─── Logs and temporary files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/

# ─── OS-specific files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Test coverage and reports ────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
.pytest_cache/

# ─── Documentation build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
docs/_build/
site/

# ─── ARCUS framework directories (never document framework internals) ─────────
.arcus/scripts/
.arcus/templates/
.github/agents/
.github/prompts/
.github/skills/

# ─── Project-specific exclusions (add yours below) ───────────────────────────
